# Frontend AI Coding Rules

**Project:** Curby - San Francisco Parking App  
**Last Updated:** January 11, 2026  
**For:** Cursor, Claude, Copilot, and all AI coding assistants

---

## 🎯 Project Context

This is a **mobile-first Progressive Web App (PWA)** for San Francisco parking regulations.
- **Focus:** Real-time parking legality checking
- **Coverage:** Mission & SOMA neighborhoods (34,292 street segments)
- **Users:** SF residents, gig workers, daily commuters

---

## 📁 Directory Structure (FOLLOW THIS)

```
frontend/
├── src/
│   ├── App.tsx              # Router setup (DO NOT move routes elsewhere)
│   ├── main.tsx             # Entry point
│   ├── globals.css          # Global Tailwind styles
│   ├── pages/               # Page components
│   │   └── Index.tsx        # Main page (default route)
│   ├── components/          # Feature components
│   │   ├── ui/             # shadcn/ui components (DO NOT EDIT)
│   │   ├── MapView.tsx     # Leaflet map component
│   │   ├── ParkingNavigator.tsx
│   │   ├── BlockfaceDetail.tsx
│   │   └── [your new components]
│   ├── types/               # TypeScript type definitions
│   ├── utils/               # Utility functions
│   ├── hooks/               # Custom React hooks
│   └── lib/                 # Third-party library configs
├── public/                  # Static assets
└── README.md
```

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack (USE THESE)

### Core Framework
- **React 18** with **TypeScript** (strict mode)
- **Vite** for build tooling
- **React Router** (routes stay in `src/App.tsx`)

### UI & Styling
- **Tailwind CSS** - Use extensively for ALL styling
- **shadcn/ui** - Pre-built UI components (already installed)
- **Lucide React** - Icons (already installed)
- **Radix UI** - Primitives (already installed via shadcn)

### Map & Location
- **Leaflet** - Map rendering
- **React Leaflet** - React bindings for Leaflet
- **OpenStreetMap** - Tile provider (free, no API key)

### PWA
- **vite-plugin-pwa** - Service worker, manifest, offline support

---

## ✅ CRITICAL RULES

### 1. File Placement (ALWAYS FOLLOW)
```
NEW PAGE? → src/pages/YourPage.tsx
NEW COMPONENT? → src/components/YourComponent.tsx
NEW TYPE? → src/types/yourTypes.ts
NEW UTILITY? → src/utils/yourUtil.ts
NEW HOOK? → src/hooks/useYourHook.ts
```

### 2. Component Visibility (IMPORTANT!)
**Problem:** Components created but not imported = user can't see them
**Solution:** ALWAYS update the parent to import and render new components
```tsx
// BAD: Create component but don't use it
// GOOD: Create component AND add to parent
import YourNewComponent from '@/components/YourNewComponent';

// In parent's JSX:
<YourNewComponent />
```

### 3. shadcn/ui Components (DO NOT EDIT)
- Components in `src/components/ui/` are from shadcn/ui
- **NEVER edit these files directly**
- If you need changes, create a NEW wrapper component
```tsx
// BAD: Edit src/components/ui/button.tsx
// GOOD: Create src/components/CustomButton.tsx that wraps Button
```

### 4. React Router (KEEP IN App.tsx)
- All routes MUST stay in `src/App.tsx`
- Do NOT create separate routing files
```tsx
// src/App.tsx
<BrowserRouter>
  <Routes>
    <Route path="/" element={<Index />} />
    <Route path="/your-page" element={<YourPage />} />
  </Routes>
</BrowserRouter>
```

### 5. TypeScript (USE STRICTLY)
- Always define types for props
- Avoid `any` - use proper types
- Use TypeScript's strict mode
```tsx
// GOOD
interface Props {
  title: string;
  count: number;
}

export function MyComponent({ title, count }: Props) {
  // ...
}

// BAD
export function MyComponent(props: any) {
  // ...
}
```

---

## 🎨 Styling Guidelines

### Tailwind CSS (PRIMARY)
- Use Tailwind for ALL styling
- Leverage utility classes extensively
- Mobile-first approach (default styles are mobile)

```tsx
// GOOD: Tailwind utilities
<div className="flex items-center gap-4 p-4 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md">

// BAD: Inline styles
<div style={{ display: 'flex', padding: '16px' }}>

// BAD: Custom CSS file for component-specific styles
```

### Responsive Design Pattern
```tsx
// Mobile-first (default)
<div className="text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg">
  // Small on mobile, larger on desktop
</div>
```

### Color System (USE PROJECT COLORS)
```tsx
// Primary colors (based on parking status)
className="bg-green-500"   // Legal parking
className="bg-red-500"     // Illegal parking
className="bg-yellow-500"  // Partial restrictions
className="bg-gray-400"    // Unknown/loading
```

